       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You're not the prescriber, and the dose is still 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe.\n\nHere's what can happen next:\n- **The treating prescriber** can enter the order themselves. They can also contact me and confirm the dose is intentional, and pharmacy would normally review it too.\n- **A corrected order** is something I can enter once a prescriber approves it. One option is ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth up to three or four times daily, within the 3,200 mg/day limit.\n\nIf this is a data-entry or billing exercise, I can help with that in some way that doesn't involve a live medication order."
